@page "/learn"

<PageTitle>Learn</PageTitle>

<div class="page-heading">
    <div>
        <div class="eyebrow">Code map</div>
        <h1>Learn from the dashboard</h1>
        <p>Use the real application as the lesson plan instead of isolated examples.</p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="lesson-grid">
    <article class="panel">
        <span class="lesson-number">01</span>
        <h2>C# + LINQ</h2>
        <p>Open <code>Policies.razor</code>. Change the filtering and ordering rules.</p>
        <code>.Where(p => p.Active)</code>
    </article>

    <article class="panel">
        <span class="lesson-number">02</span>
        <h2>Dependency injection</h2>
        <p>Compare <code>IInsuranceDataService</code>, <code>DemoInsuranceDataService</code>, and <code>ApiInsuranceDataService</code>.</p>
    </article>

    <article class="panel">
        <span class="lesson-number">03</span>
        <h2>Blazor components</h2>
        <p>Study <code>ClaimCard.razor</code> for <code>[Parameter]</code> and <code>EventCallback&lt;Claim&gt;</code>.</p>
    </article>

    <article class="panel">
        <span class="lesson-number">04</span>
        <h2>Forms + validation</h2>
        <p>Open the Create Claim form and inspect <code>EditForm</code>, input components, and DataAnnotations.</p>
    </article>

    <article class="panel">
        <span class="lesson-number">05</span>
        <h2>ASP.NET Core API</h2>
        <p>Open <code>InsuranceDashboard.Api/Program.cs</code> and trace the endpoint handlers.</p>
    </article>

    <article class="panel">
        <span class="lesson-number">06</span>
        <h2>Repositories</h2>
        <p>Follow an API endpoint into <code>IClaimsRepository</code> and <code>ClaimsRepository</code>.</p>
    </article>

    <article class="panel">
        <span class="lesson-number">07</span>
        <h2>Async / await</h2>
        <p>Trace <code>OnInitializedAsync</code> from component to HTTP request and back.</p>
    </article>

    <article class="panel">
        <span class="lesson-number">08</span>
        <h2>Next upgrades</h2>
        <p>EF Core, authentication, API gateway patterns, Web Components, tests, and MAUI can all grow from this codebase.</p>
    </article>
</div>
